---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SqlReview from '../components/SqlReview.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SQL Performance Review — Mila Business Solutions LLC"
  description="Paste a slow SQL query and get a plain-English performance review: what's likely slowing it down, which indexes would help, and a suggested rewrite."
>
  <Section narrow>
    <div class="reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Live tool</p>
      <h1 style="margin-top:var(--space-3);">SQL Performance Review</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        Paste a query that feels slow. You'll get a plain-English read on what's
        likely hurting it, which indexes would help, and a suggested rewrite.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-4);">
        This is a review, not a guarantee. Without your execution plan, table
        sizes, and existing indexes, no tool can truly <em>optimise</em> a query
        &mdash; so this one doesn't claim to. Add your schema definitions and the
        analysis gets considerably sharper.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section narrow tight>
    <SqlReview />
  </Section>

  <Section sunken narrow title="What this actually does">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h3>Good at</h3>
        <ul class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-3); padding-left:var(--space-5);">
          <li>Spotting predicates that stop an index being used</li>
          <li>Finding per-row work that could be done once</li>
          <li>Proposing a covering index from supplied DDL</li>
          <li>Explaining the problem in terms a non-DBA can act on</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Can't do</h3>
        <ul class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-3); padding-left:var(--space-5);">
          <li>See your execution plan, row counts, or data distribution</li>
          <li>Know which indexes you already have, unless you paste them</li>
          <li>Account for your hardware, contention, or statistics</li>
          <li>Replace testing a change before it goes to production</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:var(--space-6);">
      That list is the honest version. If the second column is where your real
      problem lives, that's the work we do with clients directly &mdash;
      <a href="/contact/">get in touch</a>.
    </p>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
